WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.434
-Oh, we love you.
It's so good to see you.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.200
-It's so good to see you
in person.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.000
-In person.
Yeah, last time, it was Zoom.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.167
It was Zoom.
-I know. I know.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:08.968
-I'm so happy you're here.
You look great.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.868
-Thank you.
I'm happy to be here.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.901
-We have a lot of --
We have a lot to talk about.

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.501
You're very --
-It's gonna be a long interview.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:16.367
-Yes, it's gonna be
a 45-minute interview.

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.300
[ Laughter ]
You are -- You're in the middle

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.033
of shooting season five...
-Yes.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.300
-...of "The Handmaid's Tale."

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.400
Season four, by the way,
you ended with a banger.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.400
-Oh, yes.
A bit of a bang, yes.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.067
-It was wild.
It was wild.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:29.801
-It was a lot.
-Yeah, you didn't really

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:31.200
warn me for that.
-Sorry about that.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.868
-Yeah, it was --
-I should have texted you.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.767
-Yeah, can you say
what this five --

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.601
season five is gonna be?
Is it gonna be a --

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:40.834
-We figured the physical comedy
was really working for us.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:42.467
-Yeah, that's
what it's known for.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.067
Yeah, "The Handmaid's Tale."
-The prat -- the pratfalls.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.167
-Yeah, pratfalls.
-So there's just more of that.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.667
-Spit takes.
-More spit takes.

00:00:47.667 --> 00:00:49.400
-Yeah, yeah, of course.
-We're just gonna up the fun.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.667
-Up the comedy.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:51.968
-Yeah, that's --
-It's working.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.200
You will all like it, right?
-Yes, people think --

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.400
-What people love about
"The Handmaid's Tale."

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.567
-That is not gonna happen
at all.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:00.868
You're directing more episodes
this season.

00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.400
-Yeah.
-And you were telling me

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.834
that you have someone
shadowing you.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:06.200
-Yes.
So I'm directing three episodes

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.033
this year, and I have --
When someone shadows you,

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.200
they literally shadow you.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:10.334
They follow you around,
and they --

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.934
-To learn the ropes.
-To learn the ropes

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:14.133
and learn the show.
I have a young, up-and-coming

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.300
actor named Bradley Whitford
shadowing me.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.133
Very sweet.
I wish him well in his career.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.467
-Oh, yeah.
-One day, yeah.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.901
-You think he's gonna make it?
-One day.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.234
-Yeah, exactly.
-He'll keep at it.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:26.901
He'll keep at it.
-So he's -- Bradley Whitford.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:29.901
-Yes. We wanted to welcome him
to the office.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:31.567
And we wanted to welcome him
in the style

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.868
that we felt that he deserved.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.067
-So you put it --
-And so --

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:36.634
-You made him his own desk.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.367
You gave him his own desk.
-Yes.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.868
-Right outside the office.
It's a little --

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.167
It's a child's desk.
That's him there.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:45.868
Can we zoom in?
He's got crayons.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.801
-See?
Look.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.434
-He spelled his name right.
-He's got a nice sign.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.067
He can make --
He can make notes and drawings.

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:55.834
-Construction paper
and everything, yeah.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.367
-Yeah.
-That's pretty funny, man.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.567
Is he -- Will you give him
our best, please?

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:01.834
-I absolutely will.
I adore that man.

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:04.501
-I want to talk about your new
show, "The Shining Girls."

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:06.868
This is based off of a book
of the same name.

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:09.767
Can you set up that show?
-Yes, I will do my best.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.701
So, it is about
a woman named Kirby

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:13.667
who works at the
"Chicago Sun-Times."

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.968
And she --
The show picks up

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.501
six years after she has survived
a brutal assault.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:21.934
And there is another murder
that happens in Chicago.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:24.968
The show is set in '92.
And she starts to investigate

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.234
that murder because of
the similarities between that

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.834
and her own assault.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:31.501
Now, that said, there's also
this whole other element

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.534
to the show
that she's dealing with this

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:36.767
ever-changing reality
that's happening in her life.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.567
Like, literally,
things change around her.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:43.033
So she has to figure out
why and how that's happening.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.767
And maybe the two things
are connected.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.968
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:49.234
-Yeah, yeah.
But you -- you --

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:50.234
That was a very good
explanation.

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:52.334
You act in it.
You produced it.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.434
You even directed
a few episodes of this.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.601
Hey, what is going on with you?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.100
You are so talented.
You 're just doing it all.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.200
-Glutton for punishment.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.968
-I mean, it's hard enough to --

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.234
Don't you think
it's hard enough to act?

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:03.801
-It is --
It is hard enough to act,

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.968
especially the kind of work
that I -- that I do.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.834
And, you know,
it is getting easier.

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:11.334
I will say, the directing
and acting is so hard

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:14.267
and takes up so much
of your mind

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.968
that now when
I'm just directing

00:03:15.968 --> 00:03:18.534
or I'm just acting, I'm like,
"Oh, my God, this is so easy."

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.000
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah. Right.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.634
I mean, come on.
-So when I'm acting, I'm like --

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.367
-You're Elisabeth Moss,
so you're allowed to say that.

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.100
Yeah, of course.
But I mean, do you ever

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.534
screw up a scene acting,
and you're acting,

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.334
and you mess up, and you're
like, "Sorry, everybody,"

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.467
and then you're mad at yourself?

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.467
-How dare you suggest I mess up.
-No, never!

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.167
Of course not!
No, no, no. Never!

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.067
You would never --
-How dare you.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.934
-No, you wouldn't --
"How dare you!"

00:03:37.934 --> 00:03:40.033
-Insulting!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.400
-"I've never been
more insulted in my life!"

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.100
-I mess up all the time,
but it -- it's great,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.367
'cause you get to go again.
You know what I mean?

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:45.634
-Yeah, you're like,
"Hey, that's just the --

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:47.133
that's the way it is."
-Yeah, it's not theater.

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:49.167
-"Except for you, by the way.
You gotta remember your lines."

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.033
Yeah, but everyone else
is allowed to make mistakes.

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.434
-Absolutely.
-I know that the story

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:54.968
takes place in Chicago.
-Yeah.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.767
-And you filmed it in Chicago.
-Yeah.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.100
We got to film in Chicago.
My mom's from Chicago.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.534
-I know you're a Cubs fan.
-Yeah.

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.067
-You -- yeah.
So that was good.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:07.067
I wanted to ask you a question,
because you go to the Cubs game.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.734
You order a hot dog.
What do you get on your hot dog?

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:12.501
You get...
-[ Sighs ] Ketchup,

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.367
which is very controversial.
I know.

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.901
-Wrong answer.
-I know it's the wrong answer.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.033
[ Cheering ]
-It's the wrong an--

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.734
-Well, thank you!
-No!

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.167
-Thank you!
-Let's vote on it!

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.968
-Yes, ketchup!
-Let's vote -- let's vote on it!

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:25.734
No, no, no.
We're not going to vote.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:26.801
We don't have
the clickers anymore.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:27.968
They are ready
for the ketchup vote.

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:29.200
-Yeah, they're ready
for the ketchup vote.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.234
-We have the ketchup cue.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:32.934
-There was a viral video
over the weekend.

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:34.100
Some people
thought it was gross.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.267
I don't know
what to feel about it.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.300
But it was a Yankee fans
had a very unusual way

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.033
of eating a hot dog.
Take a look at this.

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:45.634
[ Audience groans, laughs ]

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:48.601
[ Audience groaning ]

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:51.300
-Okay.
What is weird about that?

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.567
What do you think happens
in your stomach?

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.100
-No!
But you don't start there.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.868
-It's all gonna come together.
-You start here, you end there.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:04:59.968
We don't even end there,
but anyway.

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.834
-I do not think
it's that weird.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.234
-Well, let's see
how weird it is.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.868
-[ Laughing ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:10.901
♪♪

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.133
Damn it.
-What do you think?

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.000
I got -- all right.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.567
I put a little mustard
on my jam.

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:16.767
But this is gonna be --
-Do I get ketchup?

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.234
Oh, awesome.
-You got ketchup on yours, yeah.

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.601
Cheers.
-Okay, cheers!

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.000
-Nice to see ya, bud.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:29.133
-Get it in there.
Get it in there.

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:31.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:35.467
No.
No.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.634
♪♪

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.100
-No.
-No.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.167
-No.
-No, thumbs down.

00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:41.300
-It ruined everything.
-Thumbs down.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.200
That guy's insane.
-It ruined everything.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.334
Everything I thought
it would be.

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.334
-Don't do that.
-It ruined everything.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:46.801
Ruined the beer.
-Do not do it.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:49.567
-It tastes like
an old, cold hot dog.

00:05:49.567 --> 00:05:51.634
-Soggy.
-It reminds you of the ballpark.

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.834
I will say, I admit...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:55.501
Now it, kind of, took me back
to the baseball game.

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.167
-Separate's fine.
Not together.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:58.901
-Not together, no.
-No, ketchup or mustard.

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:01.267
Don't do it together.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.334
Here's Elisabeth Moss
in "Shining Girls."

00:06:03.334 --> 00:06:04.467
Take a look at this.

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:06.467
-Look these over
and see if something clicks.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:12.901
What about these?

00:06:12.901 --> 00:06:14.934
Really look.

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.300
Kirby.
-I don't know,

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.834
because I don't know
what he looks like.

00:06:22.834 --> 00:06:26.334
Okay?

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:29.200
He could be the guy at A&amp;P
bagging my milk.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.634
He could be the creep behind me.

00:06:30.634 --> 00:06:32.901
He could be the...
holding up the door.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:34.334
He's everybody.
He's nobody.

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:37.434
He's all the...time.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:38.934
-Aw, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:40.634
Elisabeth Moss!

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:44.300
"Shining Girls" premieres
